  "Description": "feature.fillet at vertices where more than three edges meet. A square pyramid (base 40x40, apex at height 20, all faces at 45 degrees) built as the intersection of two triangular roofs, and a hexagonal pyramid (apothem 20, height 20) built from three roofs rotated by 60 degrees. pyrApex: the four slope edges, r=2 - four fillets meet in the apex, no sphere fits, a vertex blend is needed. pyrBase: the four base edges (three edges at each base corner, not orthogonal). pyrAll: all eight edges. hexApex: the six slope edges of the hexagonal pyramid, six fillets in one vertex.",
